[A1] closure: t = 2^j gives t 2^-a = 2^(j-a); the family {2^j mod 3^n : j in Z} is the whole unit group (2 generates it, order 2 3^(n-1)),
     so max over a full period of j IS M(n); over a window shorter than the period it is a lower bound for M(n).
[A2] recursion vs brute-force word sum over all 6^n words (n <= 4, valuations <= 6, six exponents each, plus j = -3 at n = 3): max deviation 3.2e-16
[A3] m_1(0) = -0.500000000000-0.288675134595j; (1/3)e(1/3)+(2/3)e(2/3) = -0.500000000000-0.288675134595j; |m_1| = 0.577350269189 = 1/sqrt3 = 0.577350269190
[A4] inverse powers 2^-k mod 3^n well defined (2^-k 2^k = 1 mod 3^n at n = 5, 30, 120): True
[A5] bookkeeping: level n computes j in [-AMAX (HMAX - n), JMAX] from level n-1 values at j - a, a <= AMAX, i.e. from
     [-AMAX (HMAX - n + 1), JMAX - 1], inside the level-(n-1) window (asserted in the code); truncation a <= AMAX drops mass 2^-AMAX per level.
