[C8] error analysis: the truncated recursion is a weighted average with weights 2^-a (sum 1 - 2^-AMAX) times unimodular phases,
     hence an l^inf contraction; per level the computed value differs from the exact one by at most 2^-AMAX (dropped mass, |m| <= 1)
     plus the rounding of one 40-term complex sum with correctly rounded phases (<= ~41 eps); errors add, never amplify:
     |error at level n| <= n (2^-40 + 41 eps) = 120 * 9.19e-13 = 1.10e-10 at n = 120, against the value 4.12e-06 (relative 2.7e-05).
[C9] AMAX = 40 against AMAX = 50 (float64), max |difference| on the window: h=20: 9.7e-15, h=60: 5.3e-16, h=100: 3.4e-17, h=120: 1.1e-17  (predicted truncation gap <= n 2^-40 = 1.1e-10 at 120) [0s]
