[E2] is the pure family the largest at EVERY level 1..60? True; levels where another family ties within 1e-9: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]
[E3] reading: 2 generates the units mod 3^n, so every u is 2^k for a profinite exponent k in Z/2 x Z_3 (its discrete log is not an integer
     a family u 2^j is the pure family shifted by that 3-adic exponent, and for h beyond the window period (h >= 9 here) the seventeen
     families are seventeen windows of ~ (36 (60-h) + 160) residues each out of 2 3^(h-1) units: a sample of the unit group, not a cover.
